  "parent": "pt-BR",
  "notes": "Paulistano (São Paulo city). This is the variety of Barbosa & Albano (2004), so the spec keeps the pt-BR base and adds the two features that source gives for this variety alone. Strong /r/ is the velar fricative, 'usually voiced between voiced sounds and voiceless elsewhere' (p. 228): word-initial [x] (rato [ˈxatu]), ⟨rr⟩ [ɣ] (carro [ˈkaɣu]). A stressed vowel other than [i] takes a yod before word-final /S/ (p. 229: arroz [aɣojs], mas [majs]). Coda /R/ is the tap: 'Entre os paulistanos, o tepe é a realização predominante' (Castro 2013: 566); the retroflex belongs to the interior (pt-BR-x-caipira; Silva 2023: 70).",
  "quality": "research",
  "script_type": "alphabet",
